# Smoke test of the whole game: the hero walks up to the grunt and defeats it.
#
# The same file runs in `cargo test` without a window (tests/scenarios.rs) and against a
# running game (`shards scenario scenarios/smoke.scenario`), with the same meaning. It plays
# the way an agent plays: look, act, step until something happens, check the journal.
# The format is documented in the engine's README ("Сценарии").

seed 42

# --- 1. the world is as content says: the hero at one end, the grunt far beyond its aggro range
observe
expect result contains "e1 Hero"
expect result contains "e2 Grunt"
expect field e1 Health.current == 100
expect field e2 Health.current == 80
invariant field e1 Health.current > 0

# --- 2. walk towards the grunt; it notices the hero and comes to meet it
act move_to target=e2 within=3
expect result contains "move_to e2"
step 900 --until near:e1:e2:3.5
expect stopped "within"

# --- 3. fight until it is dead (the hero attacks again and again until its target dies)
act attack target=e2 repeat=true
expect result contains "attacking e2 with light until it dies"
step 1800 --until named:arena_cleared
expect stopped "arena_cleared"
expect journal "e2 winds up"
expect journal "e1 -> e2"
expect journal "e2 died"
expect shows e2 "dead"
expect field e2 Health.current == 0

# --- 4. the hero is still on its feet
observe
expect result contains "e1 Hero"
expect !journal "e1 died"
